Reward: {{Skin|Golden Cookie Ginger}} [[Skin]] {{Small|''(Exclusively obtainable while the [[Christmas Event]] is active)''}}

===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first task''', play normally until you find {{CI|Twisted Ginger|name=true}}, get in her sight, then try to find her again in another [[Floor]]. It should be noted that you'll likely have better luck when she is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].
*'''For the second task''', try and join a good run, or if you're skilled enough, do a solo run as the game will be fairly easier. Using {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}} and {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}} helps to speed up the [[Machine]] completion progress. A good way is to have a friend or two play the game as if you never existed, coming to you as express healing. This does force the need to have your friends have the skill to reach [[Floor]] 20, though having people you trust will be beneficial. You can also play on an alt account and have your main account be the Ginger.
*'''For the third task''', the optimal strategy is to equip {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} and have a friend or alt account get to 1 {{Heart}}, then heal. After that, you can either equip {{TI|Coin Purse|name=true}} as well and try going for a second heal or immediately restart the run. Collecting 100 {{Tape|name=true}} is really time consuming, and taking an extra few minutes to restart a run will be a lot more worth it. If you consider that strategy to be too time consuming, you can try to join a full run, better if they're below-average, and try playing with them. Their constant need of  heals make healing opportunities abundant, though if you can't collect Tapes fast enough, you may waste a lot more time.
To complete all tasks in tandem, play with a few friends and have them get to Floor 20 for you. When possible, try getting seen by Twisted Ginger if she spawns, and be utilized as a walking {{II|Health Kit|name=true}} for your team.

==Strategies==
On paper, Ginger has one of, if not, the best healer [[Abilities]] in-game, being a direct upgrade to {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}'s Ability with the bonus of average extracting potential. Her Ability, {{AI|Ginger|name=true}}, heals any Toon to full [[Health]] with 100 {{Tape|name=true}}, a really good Ability, capable of making your team last longer than normal. However, Tape collection, low mobility, low range, and the need to wind up your heal can have major setbacks, to the point that in most situations, she is the worst healer option in the game.

Usually, it's best to use your Ability when someone is at 1{{Heart}}, as any other Health level wastes some of Ginger's potential. However, there are other situations where that would not be ideal. A distracting {{CI|Looey|name=true}} would benefit from a lost Heart, so a {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} or Sprout would be a better fit for him. Another situation would be a run with {{Type|Main}} Toons being the majority. In that case, Cosmo can substitute if the team worries about {{II|Health Kit|name=true}} wastage and Sprout can substitute to utilize Tapes in a beneficial way, as well as having the capability of distracting in a pinch.

Unlike Sprout or Cosmo, Ginger's low mobility means [[Twisteds]] are an even bigger threat, with Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} being extra difficult. This also makes traversal difficult, so [[Machine]] or [[Item]] opportunities will be scarce, and therefore makes Tape collection a hurdle. However, if your team is kind enough, you may have a decent shot at collecting the Tapes. Sprout's high mobility gives him a bonus of being able to back-up distract for his team, while Ginger's only other role is extracting. Though Sprout's bad extraction does force him to only be a distractor, so if the Floor is too risky or the Sprout is too scared, his last available role, extracting, would make the run a bit long unless there’s Treadmill Machines. However, Ginger doesn't deal with the problem of bad extraction and can finish most Machines at a decent pace, though it still would be faster to let a nearby Extractor such as Shelly or Yatta do the machine instead. Despite this, if the run is operational with quick, 1 Heart heals, Sprout would still be better suited.

Due to her Stats, your form of tape collection should be different from the other 3 Toons with Tape requiring Abilities. Picking up niche or common [[Items]], as well as Tapes near the [[Elevator]] or near the distractor, when you know nobody else needs them, is a safe option, but take care that it isn't your number one priority. Pick up Tapes or Items on the way to a destination like an injured Toon, Machine, or the Elevator—use them as a supplemental income rather than a primary income. Since Ginger's speed is low, she benefits from mobility based Items, which means she can use them to move around more easily while also gaining Tapes, without it feeling like wastage. Taking advantage of your Stealth to focus on extracting in open areas or Machines near a distractor's looping area is a good choice too; other Toons with lower Stealth will be less inclined to extract such Machines, since they could be more susceptible to being chased or taking aggro. Each Machine gives you 10 Tapes if you fully fill it, so it's recommended to hone your focus on extracting, especially with the aforementioned Stealth. You can also stand just outside of the Elevator during Panic Mode to gain Tapes from encountering Twisteds, immediately running inside once you get them. Toons like {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, and {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} can facilitate Item grinding, since they can drop Items near Ginger, keeping her from wandering slowly and excessively using up Stamina.

Something to note is that unless you have the 100 Tapes, you can't highlight any Toons and even with the Tapes, can only highlight the nearest Toon granted they're close to you. Therefore, if you need to heal someone, calling out your availability makes it easier. Another way is to tell someone you want to heal them, and ask them to stay back. Running to a Toon to heal them, especially if they are quite fast, will just be a waste of time and Stamina. 

Be aware healing distractors would be quite difficult, as they usually need a lot of space, not being able to stand still to let Ginger heal them, so following the distractor would be one of the only options. The other option would be to circle the object the distractor is circling in the opposite direction, though this may still prove unsafe if there are faster Twisteds. Even so, the distractors are likely going to be faster than you, so the attempt could waste a lot of Stamina, not to mention looping distractors might make the Twisteds lock onto you and risk a Heart, especially if the Twisteds being distracted include ones that generally must be looped, such as {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Scraps|name=true}}. It is better to just wait for the Floor to end and heal them after the next Floor starts, but if the Distractor is in urgent need of healing, Ginger's various drawbacks often make it nearly impossible to heal them appropriately or in time before the Distractor dies. This could be combated if there is an available backup distractor to take over while the main one loses the Twisteds to get healed by Ginger, but if one isn't available, it could be very risky for Twisteds to be loose, especially faster ones.

One of the only situations where Ginger might be able to heal the distractor in action safely is if a distractor such as {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} or {{CI|Goob|name=true}} is solar system distracting with Bobette. This strategy often does not require an island or much space to circle around, so a Ginger could stand next to Bobette or follow Bobette's path (depending on if Bobette is still or moving) and heal that way, however there is still a chance that the distractor leaves Ginger's range due to how small it is.

Generally, Ginger isn't the best healer in more dangerous scenarios, so its a good idea to bring a Sprout or Cosmo (Cosmo is more recommended) to heal in dangerous situations, while Ginger can offer more effective healing at resting points, especially the [[Break Room]]. She acts somewhat like a medical station or hospital in comparison to the other healers. However, experience with slower Toons can make her a really good Toon.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}
Recommended [[Trinket]] combinations for Ginger:

====Survivability====
*'''{{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket enables Ginger to outrun nearly all Twisteds except {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} and any twisteds that have adjacent speeds to him before [[Panic Mode]] {{Small|(24.2 run speed)}} and helps her retain hearts. Here are some options to pair Pink Bow with: 
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to outrun Twisted Pebble before Panic Mode {{Small|(25.4 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to outrun every Twisted except {{CI|Twisted Bobette|name=true}} or similar/higher speed Twisteds during Panic Mode and assist teammates {{Small|(31.4 run speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Bone|name=true}}''', to help quickly scout for Items at the start of a new floor and allow you to collect Items faster;
***'''{{TI|Diary|name=true}}''', although quite situational, can help if there is a distractor with 4{{Star}} [[Stealth]] such as {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} so you can safely go near them to collect heals while they distract;
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to help Ginger avoid Twisteds during an [[Ichor Leak]], or while {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} on the Floor;
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction Section'''; etc.

====Extraction====
*'''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket allows Ginger to take full advantage over her 3{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]] {{Small|(1.00 extraction speed)}} and [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(100.5 skill check size)}}. Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:
***'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''', to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote, and better {{Tape|name=true}} collection;
***'''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''', to speed up [[Machine]] completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction {{Small|(25.57 avg/23.26 with Tech Savvy)}};
***Any Trinkets listed in the '''Survivability/Mobility''' section, to help with survival.

====Ability/Support====
*'''{{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}}''', to reduce {{AI|Ginger|name=true}}'s [[Ability]] cooldown {{Small|(92s)}}.
**'''{{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}}''', to further reduce '''Baked with Care!'''<nowiki/>'s cooldown, though only by a small amount as the Trinket works with units {{Small|(87s)}}.
*'''{{TI|Dandy Plush|name=true}}''', to help you buy healing Items if a [[Toon]] that needs {{Tape|name=true}} is present, letting you still have sufficient Tapes from usual activities for healing Items.

'''Note: It isn't recommended to use {{II|Tape|name=true}}-providing Trinkets such as {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} as it only provides enough for one heal, but can be useful if a teammate takes a hit on earlier floors before you have 100 Tapes. You can also use it to buy a heal from [[Dandy's Store]] should it appear, as you cannot heal yourself. Although this Trinket can be used, it is highly recommended to use a Trinket from the Mobility or Extraction sections as the Fancy Purse's effect is one-time use.'''

